  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_uv",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1068
        },
        "text": "Tiled UV and the view vector in **tangent space** — the parallax node marches along its XY component."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_pom",
        "position": {
          "x": 1294,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 762
        },
        "text": "**Parallax (steep)**: 12 layers; at each layer the height is compared to the layer depth, then the intersection is interpolated. The result is the UV where the eye ray actually hits the brick surface — every texture below is read there."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_maps",
        "position": {
          "x": 2260,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "Albedo, height and normal map are sampled at the **parallax UV**. The normal map is unpacked and scaled with *Normal Strength*."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_rough",
        "position": {
          "x": 3618,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "Height drives two cheap tricks: occlusion `lerp(1, h, strength)` darkens the joints, and smoothness is multiplied by `0.4 + 0.6·smoothstep(0.1, 0.4, h)` so mortar is rougher than brick."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 4976,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "PBR set: albedo, tangent-space normal, smoothness, occlusion."
      }
    ],
